<BaseLayout title="identity — imhotep">
  <article class="article">
    <div class="eyebrow">identity</div>
    <h1>imhotep is a lens, not a disguise.</h1>
    <p class="lede"><strong>Vishnu Unnikrishnan</strong> is the person. <em>imhotep</em> is the editorial identity for the work: engineering, architecture, products, teams, and the discipline of making complicated systems useful.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why the name</h2>
      <p>Imhotep sits at an unusual intersection of architecture, engineering, medicine, administration, and long-lived systems. The reference matters because the work here is similarly cross-disciplinary: technical depth is useful only when it creates durable outcomes.</p>
      <h2>The operating idea</h2>
      <p>Proof before claims. Trade-offs before slogans. Calm interfaces over exposed complexity. Systems that can be explained, operated, changed, and trusted.</p>
      <h2>The signature</h2>
      <p>The hieroglyphic mark appears only at the final edge of the site. It is a signature, not decoration.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
